// graph.init must never crash the process, whether or not this machine has a
// usable OpenGL driver. Without one, InitWindow() fails silently (raylib logs
// a WARNING and returns rather than aborting) — graph.init must turn that into
// a catchable error instead of returning a window that later crashes the
// process in graph.close(). Both outcomes below are correct; what this test
// actually checks is the process exit code, via run.ps1's PASS/FAIL harness.
import std graph

danger {
    dyn win = graph.init(64, 64, "graph-init-safety")
    graph.close(win)
}
print("safe")
